-- Four accounts that money passes through at different speeds.
-- The emergency fund holds a foreign currency whose rate moves, and the broker
-- spends its cash on shares whose price then moves: neither is money passing
-- through, so both stay at the bottom, largest first.  The wallet and the
-- checking account see the same ten dollars go out, but the wallet is tiny, so
-- it turns over fastest and goes on top.
currency USD 0.01
currency EUR 0.01
currency VWRL 1

account assets:broker
account assets:checking
account assets:emergency
account assets:wallet
account equity
account expenses

